      "desc:8": "Stop dragging steam pipes across the map. The Steam Hub Array is a 9x9 tower, 3 to 32 blocks tall: every layer adds 25 storage slots, up to 750 units. A plain unit holds 320M liters, reinforced 1.28G — and the Hub Singularity Chip multiplies the whole tank by 5 and unlocks node transfer.\n\nWire it into your MV line through steam hub output hatches: auto-output runs at 20,000,000 L/s, more steam than any GT machine row can drink. Your bill is recipe math, not pipe math: steam (L/s) = EUt x 10,000 / max(1,000, efficiency).\n\nHand in a formed controller and its chip to open the crossover road.",
